.\"
.\" IOCTL(2) - Substrate Native Personality
.\"
.TH IOCTL 2 "January 2026" "Substrate OS" "System Calls"
.SH NAME
ioctl \- control device
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/ioctl.h>
.PP
.BI "int ioctl(int " fd ", unsigned long " request ", ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR ioctl ()
system call manipulates the underlying device parameters of special files.
.PP
The
.I request
argument is a device-dependent request code. The third argument is an
untyped pointer to memory, traditionally
.BR "char *argp" .
.SS Terminal ioctls
For terminal devices,
.BR ioctl ()
supports the following requests:
.TP
.B TCGETS (0x5401)
Get terminal attributes into
.BR "struct termios" .
.TP
.B TCSETS (0x5402)
Set terminal attributes from
.BR "struct termios" .
.TP
.B TCSETSW (0x5403)
Set terminal attributes after output drains.
.TP
.B TCSETSF (0x5404)
Set terminal attributes after output drains and flush input.
.TP
.B TIOCGWINSZ (0x5413)
Get window size into
.BR "struct winsize" .
.TP
.B TIOCSPGRP (0x5410)
Set the foreground process group ID.
.TP
.B TIOCGPGRP (0x540F)
Get the foreground process group ID.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned.
.PP
On error, \-1 is returned, and
.I errno
is set appropriately.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EBADF
.I fd
is not a valid file descriptor.
.TP
.B ENOTTY
.I fd
is not associated with a character special device.
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I request
is not valid.
.SH NOTES
.SS Substrate Native ABI
.nf
Syscall Number: 54 (SYS_IOCTL)
Arguments:      fd, request, arg (on stack)
.fi
.SS Native termios
Substrate's native
.B struct termios
uses NCCS=32 control characters. The Linux personality translates
between this and Linux's NCCS=19 format.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR termios (4),
.BR tty (4),
.BR substrate (7)
.SH STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2001, POSIX.1-2008 (partially).
